lanes/m1-julia/redgreen.log

Red-green demonstration for the Julia smoke test, work package 1.9 (lane m1-julia's brief, point
5): two of the Julia tests of tests/julia/smoke.jl are shown to fail when the expected value is
wrong for the right reason. Both mutations are made in scratch copies of include/ and src/ under
build/redgreen/mut1/ and build/redgreen/mut2/, never in the working tree:

    rm -rf build/redgreen
    mkdir -p build/redgreen/mut1/include build/redgreen/mut1/src
    mkdir -p build/redgreen/mut2/include build/redgreen/mut2/src
    cp -r include/. build/redgreen/mut1/include/    # and mut2, and src/ the same way
    cp -r src/.     build/redgreen/mut1/src/

build/ is .gitignore'd (line 3: "build/"); nothing in the working tree (include/, src/, tests/)
was touched by either mutation. Neither mutation touches src/*.c: adelefeld's own code reads
struct fields by name, so a reordered or widened struct recompiles cleanly with no warning, and
the library's own C behaviour (arithmetic, printing) is unaffected — the point of both demos is
that a Julia binding, which reads memory by documented offset and by adf_sizeof_<type>(), not by
field name, is not so lucky.

================================================================================
DEMO 1: adf_fball_struct, fields A and H swapped. A genuine ABI-breaking change that sizeof and
_Alignof cannot see by themselves: the struct keeps size 48 and alignment 8.
================================================================================

--- mutation: build/redgreen/mut1/include/adelefeld/fball.h ---

--- include/adelefeld/fball.h
+++ build/redgreen/mut1/include/adelefeld/fball.h
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
    borrowed (conventions 4.2). */
 typedef struct
 {
-    fmpz_t A, H, d;
+    fmpz_t H, A, d;  /* MUTATION (lane m1-julia, red-green demo): A and H swapped, sizeof/alignof unchanged */
     int backend;
     const adf_modctx_struct * mctx;
     ulong * res;

--- build ---

    cc -shared -fPIC -Ibuild/redgreen/mut1/include -std=c11 -O1 -g -Wall -Wextra \
        build/redgreen/mut1/src/*.c -o build/redgreen/mut1/libadelefeld.so -lflint -lgmp -lm

Clean build, no warnings, no errors: C code names its fields, so a reorder is invisible to the
compiler and to every C test.

