Exactly 2 of the 48 checks fail, both in the adf_fball testset, both at the raw-offset reads
(tests/julia/smoke.jl:173-174): raw_A reads 12 (H's value under the true layout) instead of 3,
raw_H reads 3 instead of 12. Every other check passes, including the sizeof/alignof layout checks
(adf_fball_struct is still 48 bytes, alignment 8: unaffected by a reorder) and the get_str
comparisons ("(* ; 3 mod 12)", "(* ; 2 mod 6)", "(* ; 3 mod 6)" are unchanged, because the
library's own printer reads x->A and x->H by name, wherever the compiler puts them). This is
exactly why a sizeof/alignof check alone is not enough for a binding that reads fields directly,
and why tests/julia/layouts.jl also carries the field offsets of adf_fball_struct.

