  a context: adf_modctx_new_blocks, nblocks, block, free                 |    4            4  0.0s

Exactly 1 of the 48 checks fails: the layouts testset's adf_rat_struct row
(tests/julia/smoke.jl:99), got_size 0x18 (24, decimal) against the documented want_size 16 of
tests/julia/layouts.jl. This is exactly the fault CV-40 (docs/conventions.md 12.4) exists to turn
into a load-time error instead of memory corruption: a binding that had allocated
adf_sizeof_rat() bytes before this fix would have used the library's true (larger) struct size
correctly, but a binding that hard-coded 16 bytes from stale documentation, without ever calling
adf_sizeof_rat(), would have under-allocated and corrupted adjacent memory the first time the
library wrote the extra field. The mutation demonstrates why layouts.jl (and this comparison in
smoke.jl) exists, not merely that the library's own function works.

